Text:
fearlessOnClick is a helper program that mediate between the desk behaviour on double clicks on files and fearlessMessage Message.

Story:
A event The desk opens the file x with fearlessOnClick, and x is a .fearless file.
B action fearlessOnClick runs fearlessMessage "Register b", for b the Base16 of the path of the folder holding x.
C action fearlessOnClick runs fearlessMessage "Show".

Story:
A event The desk opens the file x with fearlessOnClick, and x is not a .fearless file.
B action fearlessOnClick runs fearlessMessage "OpenWithOrShortcut b", for b the Base16 of the path of x.

Story:
A action fearlessOnClick runs fearlessMessage "Message".
B after fearlessMessage prints the Answer Refused, with Error.
C action fearlessOnClick shows Error in a dialog.//no? only the fearlessManager should ever use dialogs here.

Story:
A action fearlessOnClick runs fearlessMessage Message.
B after fearlessMessage prints standard error XXX, and ends with an error. //what if it then ends with no error?
C action fearlessOnClick shows e in a dialog.//no

Implementation notes:
Reconciliator$reconcile will receive the OS path pointing to the program location of fearlessOnClick.
In this way the desk opens the files of the extensions that the manager holds with fearlessOnClick.
On macOS the desk hands the files to open to fearlessOnClick in an open event; on the other desks the desk runs fearlessOnClick with the path of each file as an argument.
